                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">The United Nations</hi>: <list>
                            <item>General United States–United Nations relations: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg1">I. United States foreign policy in the
                                            United Nations setting</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg46">II. Problems arising under the United
                                            States–United Nations headquarters agreement of 1947,
                                            and related matters</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>General organizational questions affecting the United Nations and
                                of particular interest to the United States: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg78">I. The election to fill the Security
                                            Council seat being vacated by vacated by
                                            Yugoslavia</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg135">II. The question of placing the
                                            Egyptian item regarding Morocco on the final agenda of
                                            the General Assembly</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg162">III. The question of the scale of
                                            national assessments for the apportionment of the
                                            expenses of the regular (administrative) budget of the
                                            United Nations</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg209">United States policy regarding problems arising
                                    from the question of the representation of China in the organs
                                    of the United Nations</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg286">United States policy regarding the admission of
                                    new members to the United Nations; the question of the admission
                                    of Italy as a special case</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>Attitude of the United States toward Soviet peace propaganda at
                                the United Nations, and related matters: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg455">I. “Threats” by the Soviet Union to
                                            leave the United Nations</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg477">II. The two Soviet “peace” items at the
                                            Sixth Regular Session of the General Assembly: (1)
                                            “Measures To Combat the Threat of a New World War,” etc.
                                            (the old Soviet item); (2) “Complaint of Aggressive Acts
                                            of the United States and Its Interference in the
                                            Domestic Affairs of Other Countries,” etc. (the new
                                            Soviet item)</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg497">III. The complaint by Yugoslavia of
                                            hostile activities on the part of the Soviet Union and
                                            other countries of Eastern Europe</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>Matters arising under Chapters XI, XII, and XIII of the Charter of
                                the United Nations (Trusteeship and Non-Self-Governing Territories): <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg520">I. The Ewe question in the Trusteeship
                                            Council</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg607">II. Consultations on dependent area
                                            questions with non-administering members of the United
                                            Nations</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg623">III. Bilateral talks on colonial policy
                                            with the United Kingdom (London) and France (Paris),
                                            October 1951</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg655">IV. Questions concerning the competence
                                            of the General Assembly and the Fourth Committee in
                                            regard to dependent areas</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg673">V. The South West Africa question</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <pb facs="0010" n="VI" xml:id="pgVI"/>
                            <item>Human rights questions in the United Nations setting: the United
                                States position: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg735">I. The draft international covenant on
                                            human rights</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg772">II. Proposals for the right of peoples
                                            and nations to self-determination</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg789">III. The draft convention on freedom of
                                            information</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg821">IV. Matters respecting refugees and
                                            stateless persons</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg842">V. The question of the treatment of
                                            people of Indian origin in the Union of South
                                            Africa</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
